/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-76-
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-77-  // ==== return / pop the frame (the returned expr evaluates by strictness) ==
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-78-  rule <k> Return(V:Val) ~> _ => #pop </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-79-       <ret> noRet => retV(V) </ret>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k:80:  rule <k> #endcall => #pop ... </k>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-81-       <ret> noRet => retV(noneV) </ret>
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-82-  // pop: restore env, DEALLOCATE the callee frame, and wind scopeLoc back (LIFO allocation
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-83-  // makes the saved loc the callee frame's own loc). Sound because no closureVal outlives its
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-84-  // defining frame (frontend subset: no returned/stored closures; module defs live in loc 0).
/reference/k-proof/reference-semantics/semantics/functions.k-85-  rule <k> #pop => V ~> CONT </k>
