codex
I found the concrete environment defect: this container’s `/proc` mount is from a different PID namespace. Lean 4.22 calls `readlink("/proc/<getpid>/exe")`, which fails here, while `/proc/self/exe` works; that breaks Lean before it parses any file. I’m applying a narrow temporary preload shim that rewrites only the current-process `/proc/<pid>/exe` lookup to `/proc/self/exe`. It does not touch source, theorem checking, file reads, or proof behavior.
apply patch
